# @fractal/singularity — the point where a tree of possibilities collapses
# into a single artifact; the settled-point in phase space toward which
# @paradox/spiral dynamics converge; the small-scale mathematical analog
# (at fractal altitude) of what @paradox/spiral names at dynamics altitude.
#
# Third species-decl of the @fractal family (siblings: mandelbrot,
# crystal). Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara per Alex 2026-07-20 in-transcript
# Q2 ratification.
#
# === Alex 2026-07-20 verbatim (load-bearing) ===
#
#   > "collapse collapse.rs into singularity.rs"
#
# Q2 ratified the verbatim name `singularity` at both `rust/fractal/src/`
# AND at `shards/fractal/`. Mara Refinement 1 rename (singularity →
# collapse) is CANCELLED per Alex direct-transcript adjudication. The
# fractal-altitude migration boundary preserves the source name; two-tick
# discipline (readable name over foundational per @cyberpunk namespace
# migration precedent). Landing D adjudication landed in canonical spec
# `docs/specs/paradox-family-and-cyberpunk-intervention.md` §7 (commit
# `1cb9dc1`) with Split-C recommendation (C1 verbatim migration at
# rust/fractal/; C2 rust/singularity/ crate scaffold for black-hole
# physics research outlet).
#
# This substrate-decl is the LEAD before Reed's code migration cascade
# per substrate-decl-leads discipline. The mint declares the species
# shape; Reed's post-mint work materializes the ~600 LOC Rust body at
# `rust/fractal/src/singularity.rs` from the fragmentation source.
#
# === What @fractal/singularity IS ===
#
# The species that carries the Singularity trait shape (per
# `/Users/reed/dev/projects/fragmentation/src/singularity.rs`) at
# substrate-decl altitude:
#
#   Singularity {
#     collapse() -> Artifact       # tree → single settled artifact
#     settle(artifact) -> Self     # artifact → reconstructed tree
#   }
#
# Two implementations at fragmentation altitude anchor the two rungs
# of the optics hierarchy at species altitude:
#
#   - `Iso` (identity): `Singularity for Fractal<E, H>` — collapse=clone,
#     settle=clone. No information loss. No dimensional reduction. The
#     trivial case: a black hole with zero mass; no event horizon; full
#     recovery because nothing happened. Observer-independent.
#
#   - `Lens` (witnessed): `WitnessedSingularity<'a, H, R>` — collapse
#     writes a commit whose node is a Lens targeting the original tree.
#     The observer (committer) is part of the commit but NOT part of
#     the Lens target. Different observer → different commit SHA; same
#     tree → same Lens target OID. MARA doctrine grounding: witnessed =
#     committer-in-hash-not-tree (the observer is in the COMMIT, not
#     the TREE).
#
# Two rungs above (Prism, Traversal) admit partial-measurement and
# radiation-chain semantics per fragmentation research doc
# `docs/research/singularity-rabbit.md`; forward-promised at species
# altitude for a follow-up tick when compositional consumers surface
# the need. The Iso + Lens shape below carries the two load-bearing
# implementations empirically anchored in fragmentation source.
#
# === Kin-to-@paradox/spiral (load-bearing composition edge) ===
#
# @paradox/spiral names the DYNAMICS-carrier at species altitude
# (`spiral = process`: trigger → spiraling-motion; unstable attractor
# with strong basin). @fractal/singularity names the SETTLED-POINT in
# phase space toward which that dynamics converges — the mathematical
# analog (at fractal altitude) of what @paradox/spiral names at
# dynamics altitude.
#
# Composition edge: the singularity that sits at the bottom of a
# @paradox/spiral trajectory IS a @fractal/singularity carrier at
# fractal altitude. The `wound_oid` field of @paradox/spiral's
# spiral_state (per `shards/paradox/spiral.mirror` §spiral_state)
# resolves to a @paradox/trauma Crystal whose Crystal-shape at
# @fractal/crystal altitude IS the collapse-artifact of a
# @fractal/singularity operation on the wound-substrate.
#
# Symmetry: @paradox/spiral is the DYNAMICS altitude naming;
# @fractal/singularity is the STATIC-SHAPE altitude naming. Both point
# at the same substrate phenomenon — the collapse-under-observation.
# @paradox/spiral tracks the TRAJECTORY toward collapse; this species
# tracks the COLLAPSE-EVENT itself + the Lens-back-to-source recovery
# discipline.
#
# === Optics hierarchy ↔ information recovery (fragmentation §Optics) ===
#
# The four rungs (Iso / Lens / Prism / Traversal) map to information-
# recovery bounds:
#
#   Iso        — unitarity; full reversible recovery; no collapse.
#   Lens       — focused, total; single observation; observer-in-commit.
#   Prism      — partial, may fail; one Hawking quantum per observation.
#   Traversal  — accumulated partial; the Hawking radiation chain.
#
# Fragmentation source implements Iso (`impl Singularity for Fractal`)
# and Lens (`WitnessedSingularity::collapse/settle`); Prism
# (`WitnessedSingularity::prism` returning `Option`) and Traversal
# (`WitnessedSingularity::traversal` over a chain of commits) are
# provided at the WitnessedSingularity impl surface. The species-decl
# below carries the Iso + Lens invariants at bilateral altitude;
# Prism + Traversal are forward-promised (Reed post-mint materialization
# territory).
#
